    feat(http): per-route read ledger + query endpoint (OBS-DUCKBRAIN-001)
    
    Reads were invisible — writes have SUPA-2 _audit ledgers and the server
    denial ledger, but nothing recorded a query. Additive, JSONL-doctrine
    observability (no SQLite):
    
    - src/http/readLedger.ts: durable append-only JSONL ledger under
      .duckbrain-audit/reads.jsonl. Row shape {ts, route, method, ns, status,
      dur_ms}; route is a NORMALIZED TEMPLATE ("GET /api/memories/key/:key"),
      so real key/id/ns values, query strings, tokens and content never reach
      the ledger. Rotation seals the active segment into zero-padded monotonic
      reads.NNNN.jsonl segments (auditLedger.ts basis) instead of a single .1
      slot — a two-rotation scenario loses no rows by construction. Reads
      traverse sealed segments oldest-first, then the active file; a torn line
      is counted (skipped_malformed) and skipped, never fatal. Appends chain
      on a serialized promise tail (the denial-auditor pattern) and failures
      are logged + swallowed, so telemetry can never break a served response.
    - src/http/middleware/readLedger.ts: GET/HEAD-only middleware recording
      exactly the documented read routes (memories, keys, namespaces, ns
      tables, activity, events stats); writes, /health, /stats, unknown
      routes, the realtime SSE stream and the /api/reads surface itself are
      never recorded (no self-recording). Mounted BEFORE authMiddleware:
      authMiddleware answers 401 without calling next(), so a ledger mounted
      after it would never see an auth-failed read; the middleware uses only
      path/method/query, never the principal, so mounting early is safe.
    - src/http/routes/reads.ts: GET /api/reads?from=&to=&route=&ns= —
      aggregates the durable ledger over an arbitrary historical window
      (inclusive epoch-ms bounds; a window entirely older than process uptime
      answers from disk). Auth-gated like sibling mounts; scoped principals
      are confined to their grants (DB-GAP-062 doctrine: ungranted ns rows
      excluded, null-ns rows visible); bad params are 400 VALIDATION_ERROR,
      never a silently narrowed window. The response carries files_read and
      skipped_malformed so ledger coverage gaps stay visible.
    
    Tests: unit (append/read-back/rotation/normalization/no-secrets),
    integration over the real createHttpServer app (window including the
    requests; acceptance window OLDER than process uptime; writes/health/
    stats/unknown produce no rows; auth-failed reads recorded with 401;
    real key values never appear in the ledger file), plus the barrel
    export assertion. Acceptance: pnpm tsc --noEmit clean, pnpm
    build:cli + pnpm build clean, targeted suites green.
    
    ch:trace row=OBS-DUCKBRAIN-001 test=src/http/readLedger.test.ts
    
